srow(355, 27, 'MATERIAL', f'"THERE IS NONE LIKE THE GOD OF JESHURUN" (33:26) — ISRAEL SAY "THERE IS NONE LIKE GOD" AND THE HOLY SPIRIT SAYS "THE GOD OF JESHURUN"; ISRAEL SAY "WHO IS LIKE YOU AMONG THE GODS, O LORD" (Exodus 15:11) AND THE HOLY SPIRIT "HAPPY ARE YOU, O ISRAEL, WHO IS LIKE YOU" (33:29); ISRAEL SAY "HEAR, O ISRAEL, THE LORD OUR GOD, THE LORD IS ONE" (6:4) AND THE HOLY SPIRIT "AND WHO IS LIKE YOUR PEOPLE ISRAEL, ONE NATION" (1 Chronicles 17:21); ISRAEL "AS AN APPLE TREE AMONG THE TREES OF THE WOOD" (Song of Songs 2:3) AND THE SPIRIT "AS A LILY AMONG THORNS" (2:2); ISRAEL "THIS IS MY GOD AND I WILL GLORIFY HIM" (Exodus 15:2) AND THE SPIRIT "THIS PEOPLE I FORMED FOR MYSELF" (Isaiah 43:21); ISRAEL "FOR YOU ARE THE GLORY OF THEIR STRENGTH" (Psalm 89:18) AND THE SPIRIT "ISRAEL, IN WHOM I WILL BE GLORIFIED" (Isaiah 49:3). ({SP_(355, 27, "ישראל", "אומרים", "אין", "כאל", "ורוח", "הקדש", "אומרת")} "Israel say: there is none like God; and the Holy Spirit says"; {SP_(355, 27, "אשריך", "ישראל", "מי", "כמוך")} "happy are you, O Israel, who is like you"): THE SIX ANTIPHONS — the chapter\'s own two verses paired (33:26 Israel\'s, 33:29 the Spirit\'s — 355:27 cites both, seated at 33:26, the first), Exodus 15:11 and 15:2 on the tape (RUN CITATIONS — the song at the Sea\'s compiled span), 6:4 the seat that read this row at chapter 6 (the Shema); the Prophets\' and the Writings\' seats cited, never read; the translator sends to the Mekhilta. The compile: a status on the mutual praise (reference; the ink: "who is like you" the one phrase with psalm seats beside it). DV33-10. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 6\'s reading — 6:4).')
srow(355, 28, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO RIDES UPON THE HEAVEN AS YOUR HELP" — WHEN ISRAEL ARE UPRIGHT AND DO THE WILL OF THE PLACE, "HE RIDES UPON THE HEAVEN AS YOUR HELP"; WHEN THEY DO NOT DO HIS WILL, AS IT WERE, "IN HIS EXCELLENCY ON THE SKIES". ({SP_(355, 28, "כשישראל", "ישרים", "עושים", "רצונו", "של", "מקום")} "when Israel are upright and do the will of the Place"; {SP_(355, 28, "כביכול", "ובגאותו", "שחקים")} "as it were, in His excellency on the skies"): THE VERSE\'S TWO HALVES TWO CONDITIONS — Jeshurun read "upright" (yesharim), the rider the help when Israel are upright, the skies\' pride when not (346:2\'s "as it were" the form). The compile: a status conditional on Israel\'s deeds (the tape\'s blessing/curse rule the twin, 28\'s compiled arms cited). DV33-10. Fresh.')
srow(355, 29, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND IN HIS EXCELLENCY ON THE SKIES" — ALL ISRAEL GATHERED TO MOSES: OUR MASTER MOSES, TELL US WHAT IS THE MEASURE OF GLORY ABOVE? — FROM THE LOWER HEAVENS YOU KNOW THE MEASURE OF GLORY ABOVE. ({SP_(355, 29, "אמר", "לנו", "מה", "היא", "מדת", "כבוד", "למעלה")} "tell us what is the measure of glory above"; {SP_(355, 29, "מן", "השמים", "התחתונים")} "from the lower heavens"): THE MEASURE OF GLORY — the question to Moses (307\'s twin on the measure of judgment at chapter 32, the translator notes). The compile: no law. DV33-10. Fresh.')
srow(355, 30, 'MATERIAL', f'A PARABLE: ONE SAID, I WISH TO SEE THE KING\'S GLORY — GO TO THE CITY AND YOU WILL SEE HIM; HE SAW A CURTAIN SPREAD OVER THE CITY\'S GATE WITH PRECIOUS STONES AND PEARLS SET IN IT AND COULD NOT MOVE HIS EYES FROM IT UNTIL HE FELL; THEY SAID: IF FROM A CURTAIN AT THE GATE YOU COULD NOT MOVE YOUR EYES UNTIL YOU FELL, HAD YOU ENTERED THE CITY HOW MUCH MORE — THEREFORE "IN HIS EXCELLENCY ON THE SKIES". ({SP_(355, 30, "מבקש", "אני", "לראות", "כבודו", "של", "מלך")} "I wish to see the glory of the king"; {SP_(355, 30, "וראה", "וילון", "פרוס", "על", "פתח", "המדינה")} "and he saw a curtain spread over the gate of the city"): THE CURTAIN AT THE GATE — the a-fortiori (qal vachomer, I1) from the gate\'s curtain to the king within: the skies the curtain, the glory beyond; the piska\'s last row (the parable E26). The compile: no law. DV33-10. Fresh.')
srow(356, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE ETERNAL GOD IS A DWELLING PLACE" (33:27) — THREE SCROLLS WERE FOUND IN THE TEMPLE COURT: ONE OF "DWELLINGS" (ME\'ONIM), ONE OF "SHE-SHE", AND ONE CALLED THE SCROLL OF THE "YOUNGSTERS" (ZA\'ATUTIM); IN ONE WAS WRITTEN "A DWELLING (MA\'ON) OF THE ETERNAL GOD" AND IN TWO "A DWELLING PLACE (ME\'ONAH)" — THE SAGES ANNULLED THE ONE AND UPHELD THE TWO; IN ONE NINE "SHE" (HI) AND IN TWO ELEVEN — THE SAGES ANNULLED THE ONE AND UPHELD THE TWO; IN ONE "AND HE SENT THE YOUNGSTERS OF THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL" AND "TO THE YOUNGSTERS", IN TWO "THE YOUNG MEN" (Exodus 24:5) AND "THE NOBLES" (24:11) — THE SAGES ANNULLED THE ONE AND UPHELD THE TWO. ({SP_(356, 1, "שלשה", "ספרים", "נמצאו", "בעזרה")} "three scrolls were found in the court"; {SP_(356, 1, "ואחד", "נקרא", "ספר", "זעטוטים")} "and one was called the scroll of the youngsters"; {SP_(356, 1, "בטלו", "חכמים", "את", "האחד", "וקימו", "השנים")} "the sages annulled the one and upheld the two"): THE THREE SCROLLS OF THE COURT — the Torah\'s text fixed by the majority of three exemplars at three places, this verse\'s "dwelling place" the first (the reading of 33:27\'s first word decided by two scrolls against one — THE INK\'S OWN FORM a ruling of the court: the DB reads me\'onah, the upheld form), the spelled "she" for "he" (the ketiv-qere class — the store\'s doublings at 33:2 and 33:9 the same class), Exodus 24:5 and 24:11 on the tape (RUN CITATIONS — the young men and the nobles the upheld words); the translator: Avot deRabbi Natan and the Jerusalem Talmud\'s Taanit 4:2 the parallels (cited). The compile: the head row on 33:27 — a DATA row on the text\'s fixing (the readback\'s program is the upheld text; no law). DV33-10. Fresh.')
srow(356, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND UNDERNEATH ARE THE EVERLASTING ARMS" — IT TEACHES THAT THE LAND OF ISRAEL IS THE STRENGTH OF THE WORLD. ({SP_(356, 2, "מלמד", "שארץ", "ישראל", "היא", "תקפה", "של", "עולם")} "it teaches that the land of Israel is the strength of the world"): THE ARMS THE LAND — the world\'s underpinning read as the land (Onkelos reads the Memra\'s making of the world, 33:27\'s row — two readings); "strength" (tokef) the Hebrew of the song\'s Aramaic takifa. The compile: no law. DV33-10. Fresh.')
