srow(356, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"ALONE" — NOT AS THE "ALONE" MOSES SAID, "THE LORD ALONE LED HIM" (32:12), NOR AS THE "ALONE" JEREMIAH SAID, "I SAT ALONE BECAUSE OF YOUR HAND" (Jeremiah 15:17), BUT AS THE "ALONE" THAT WICKED ONE SAID: "LO, A PEOPLE THAT DWELLS ALONE" (Numbers 23:9). ({SP_(356, 5, "לא", "כבדד", "שאמר", "משה")} "not as the alone Moses said"; {SP_(356, 5, "אלא", "כבדד", "שאמר", "אותו", "רשע")} "but as the alone that wicked one said"): THREE "ALONES" — 32:12\'s (the seat that read this row at chapter 32; the pointer 20b owed at 32:12\'s twin paid by the reading here), Jeremiah\'s (cited, never read), Balaam\'s (Numbers 23:9 on the tape — a RUN CITATION): the word\'s sense chosen by the shelf, Israel apart among the nations. The compile: a status on Israel\'s dwelling apart (reference). DV33-11. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 32\'s reading — 32:12).')
