srow(356, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"HAPPY ARE YOU, O ISRAEL, WHO IS LIKE YOU" (33:29) — ISRAEL SAY "WHO IS LIKE YOU AMONG THE GODS" (Exodus 15:11) AND THE HOLY SPIRIT "HAPPY ARE YOU, O ISRAEL"; ALL ISRAEL GATHERED TO MOSES: TELL US WHAT GOOD THE HOLY ONE WILL GIVE US IN THE TIME TO COME — I DO NOT KNOW WHAT TO TELL YOU; HAPPY ARE YOU, WHAT IS PREPARED FOR YOU! A PARABLE OF A MAN WHO HANDED HIS SON TO A TUTOR WHO LED HIM ABOUT: ALL THESE TREES ARE YOURS, THESE VINES, THESE OLIVES — WEARY OF SHOWING HIM, HE SAID: I DO NOT KNOW WHAT TO TELL YOU; HAPPY ARE YOU, WHAT IS PREPARED FOR YOU — SO MOSES: "HOW GREAT IS YOUR GOODNESS WHICH YOU HAVE LAID UP FOR THEM THAT FEAR YOU" (Psalm 31:20). ({SP_(356, 9, "איני", "יודע", "מה", "אומר", "לכם", "אשריכם", "מה")} "I do not know what to tell you; happy are you, what"; {SP_(356, 9, "משל", "לאדם", "שמסר", "את", "בנו", "לפידגוג")} "a parable of a man who handed his son to a tutor"): THE TUTOR\'S GARDEN — the antiphon repeated (355:27), the reward beyond telling (Psalm 31:20 cited, never read — the translator\'s seat for 20b\'s "laid up in store" the sister); the parable (E26); the row seats at 33:29. The compile: no law. DV33-11. Fresh.')
